<title>INDIA: India forex reserves slip to $23.9 bln on Jan 17.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves slip to $23.9 bln on Jan 17.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves slipped to $23.9 billion on January 17, 1997 from $23.95 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Jan 17	 Jan 10	Jan 19</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	  1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,646	19,694	 16,765</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,246	 4,246	  4,457</p>
<p>    SDRs				     6	     6	    311</p>
<p>    Total			     23,898	23,946	 21,533</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
